chance accuracy: 1/12 = 0.0833
eval batch: 1024 sequences, seed=1
note: the second half of every sequence is an exact repeat of the first, so 'induction accuracy' as usually defined lumps together positions solvable by a fixed HALF_LEN positional offset (no content matching needed) with positions that repeat by chance at no fixed offset (the actual test of content-based induction). Both are reported separately below.

baseline A: 2-layer model at random initialization (untrained)
